---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

const { name, email, street, city, country } = SITE.owner;
const updated = '17 November 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description={`How ${SITE.name} handles your data.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">Datenschutzerklärung</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Short version: this blog has no analytics. Ads are shown through Google AdSense, and personalized ads only
        with your consent. The details are below.
      </p>

      <h2>Controller</h2>
      <p>
        The person responsible for this website under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:
      </p>
      <p>
        {name}<br />
        {street}<br />
        {city}, {country}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>

      <h2>Visiting the website</h2>
      <p>
        When you open a page, your browser sends technical information to the server this site runs on: your IP
        address, the page you asked for, the date and time, and your browser type. This is needed to deliver the
        page to you (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, legitimate interest in running the website). The server does not keep access
        logs, and this information is not combined with any other data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fonts, images and the site's own scripts come from this website's own server. The only content loaded from
        another company by default is Google's advertising and consent script (see "Advertising (Google AdSense)"
        below). YouTube videos only load if you choose to play one (see below).
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This website is hosted by Contabo GmbH, Welfenstrasse 22, 81541 Munich, Germany. The provider processes the
        data needed to deliver the pages on my behalf, under a data processing agreement (Art. 28 GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not use analytics. Google AdSense uses cookies and similar technologies for advertising, as
        described under "Advertising (Google AdSense)" below. The comment system also sets cookies when you add your
        name to write a comment (see below).
      </p>

      <h2>Your crochet progress</h2>
      <p>
        When you tick off rounds in a pattern, your progress is saved in your own browser (so-called local storage)
        so it's still there next time. It never leaves your device and is not sent to the server. You can clear it
        with the "Clear all ticks" button on the pattern or by clearing your browser data. This storage is strictly
        necessary for the feature you asked for (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).
      </p>

      <h2>Comments</h2>
      <p>
        Comments run on Remark42, a comment system hosted on this website's own server (comments.knittedstorybears.com).
        When you write a comment, the name you enter, your comment and the time it was posted are stored and shown
        publicly under the pattern. You only give a name: there are no accounts and no sign-in with other services.
        Remark42 keeps only a user ID and a user name; the ID and name are stored in scrambled (hashed) form. To
        remember your name, it sets two cookies: a login token and a random security token. There is no tracking.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis is your consent when you post a comment (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR). Comments stay online until you ask
        for them to be removed. You can download or delete everything the comment system knows about you from its
        settings, or email me.
      </p>
      <p>
        Comments written on the old Blogger version of this blog were moved here and are shown under each pattern,
        with the name the commenter used at the time. If one of them is yours and you'd like it removed, email me.
      </p>

      <h2>YouTube videos</h2>
      <p>
        Some patterns include a video hosted on YouTube (Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street,
        Dublin 4, Ireland). The video only loads when you press "Play video". It then loads from
        youtube-nocookie.com, and YouTube receives your IP address and information about your browser. Google may
        process this data in the USA. The legal basis is your consent, given by pressing play (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).
        Details:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising (Google AdSense)</h2>
      <p>
        This website shows ads through Google AdSense, a service of Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow
        Street, Dublin 4, Ireland ("Google"). AdSense uses cookies and similar technologies, your IP address and device
        information to show ads, limit how often you see them, measure their performance and prevent fraud.
        Personalized ads are only shown if you consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you first visit, Google's consent message (a certified consent management platform based on the IAB
        Transparency &amp; Consent Framework) asks for your choice. Legal basis: your consent, Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR and
        § 25(1) TDDDG. You can change or withdraw your consent at any time via "Privacy settings" in the footer; this
        does not affect processing done before.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google may process data in the USA. Google LLC is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework (adequacy
        decision, Art. 45 GDPR).
      </p>
      <p>
        More information:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
        and
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener" target="_blank"
          >https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a
        >
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        Links to Instagram, Ravelry, Pinterest, Facebook, YouTube and my shops on Etsy, Amigurumi.com and LoveCrafts
        are plain links. Nothing is sent to those services until you click one; after that, their own privacy
        policies apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact by email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email me, I process your address and message to answer you (Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR). My email is
        provided by Fastmail Pty Ltd, Melbourne, Australia. Transfers to Australia and other countries outside the EU
        are protected by the EU Standard Contractual Clauses. I delete messages once they are no longer needed, unless
        I am required to keep them by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact form</h2>
      <p>
        If you use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, I receive your name, email address and message. They are
        sent from this website's server to my email inbox (Fastmail, see above) and are not stored on the website. I
        use them only to answer you (Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR) and delete them once they are no longer needed, unless I
        am required to keep them by law. To block repeated spam, the server keeps your IP address in memory for at
        most one hour; it is not written to disk or logged.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access the personal data stored about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to
        restrict its processing, to receive it in a portable format, and to object to its processing (Art. 15–21
        GDPR). You can withdraw consent at any time, with effect for the future. Just email me at
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You also have the right to complain to a data protection supervisory authority, for example the one in the
        country or German state where you live.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: 2.5em;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
